# Installed Agency, Copilot CLI and Local Model Answers

Status: DONE
Milestone: A4 Provider-selectable answers before Azure
Dependencies: 28_QUESTION_DRAFTS.todo

## Purpose

Use an installed Copilot CLI now while retaining an independent future Azure adapter. Distinguish
a local CLI process using GitHub cloud models from genuine local-model inference.

## Tasks

- [x] Research installed CLI help and current public programmatic/provider contracts.
- [x] Add provider-independent exact-text requests and bounded request-ID/sequence/terminal state.
- [x] Implement and exercise a constrained noninteractive CLI adapter with no tool execution.
- [x] Support an explicitly configured loopback local-model endpoint without cloud fallback.
- [x] Integrate streamed plain text, Cancel/Copy and hide/clear/close lifecycle in the same HWND.
- [x] Provide setup, separate authentication/profile and privacy/retention guidance.
- [x] Exercise fake/model-protocol/CLI/error/cancel and synthetic UI behavior without real meeting data.
- [x] Run the single synthetic Copilot cloud prompt explicitly authorized by the owner (failed); separately authorized Agency probe succeeded.
- [x] Update the illustrated handbook, screenshots, visual README and public JOURNAL.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Only explicit Ask sends ExactText; source refs, notes, audio and unrelated transcripts stay local.
- [x] No app-initiated Ask-time sign-in; Agency never calls login. External wrapper auth expiry remains a documented limit.
- [x] No provider fallback; cloud/offline meaning is visible and setup failures remain actionable.
- [x] Completion requires terminal success; bounded partial answers survive cancellation/failure.
- [x] Local retention by the external CLI is documented, not misrepresented as memory-only operation.
- [x] Azure and Mic commit remain separate future work; Docker stays last.

